## Start

```bash
gin-kit db up
gin-kit run
```

The server runs at `http://localhost:8080`.{{if eq .ProjectType "runtime"}} In development, interactive API
docs are live at `http://localhost:8080/docs`.{{end}}

The generated runtime includes request IDs, security headers, body limits,
trusted-proxy handling, graceful shutdown, SQL-backed readiness checks, and
endpoint-class rate limiting. Review `.env.example` before deploying.

## Commands

```bash
gin-kit run                # serve with .env loaded
gin-kit build              # production binary
gin-kit check              # gofmt report + tests + vet
gin-kit routes             # print the routing table
gin-kit generate resource <Name> --fields "title:string,done:bool"
gin-kit db up|seed|status
gin-kit doctor
gin-kit explain architecture
```

`generate resource` renders a full vertical slice — domain, DTOs,
repository, service, handler, factory, tests, and migration — and prints the
wiring snippet to paste into `internal/app/app.go`.
